[Music]  is there a chance dick grayson could  soon be making his way to the world of  the batman what hint did the movie drop  that implied he could keep watching to  find out about this comics easter egg  director matt reeves as the batman  delivers a brand new version of the  caped crusader to the big screen sure dc  fans are incredibly familiar with bruce  wayne's origin after seeing it several  times in animation and live action but  this is a much darker film that takes a  precise look at the tortured vigilante a  couple of years into his crime fighting  career  the film has already been a huge hit  with critics daily star's andy lee calls  it a gritty pacy and achingly stylish  adventure while the digital fixes tom  percival says it's surprisingly hopeful  it's fair to say that this new take on  gotham city does feel grimier than  previous iterations of the bat's home  turf  it's stylistically similar to the world  of david fincher's seven with hints of  zodiac in there for good measure this  largely stems from paul dano's haunting  depiction of the riddler as a terrifying  serial killer who takes aim at the  corrupt gotham elite  thankfully robert pattinson's bruce  isn't alone in his mission to serve  justice on city streets he's also joined  by anti-hero catwoman played by zoe  kravitz and police lieutenant james  gordon played by jeffrey wright the film  isn't crammed with easter eggs like  other comic book movies that dominate  the box office but there are a few  carefully placed references to classic  dc characters the plot itself takes cues  from classic batman storylines such as  year one the long halloween and zero  year but there's also a surprising nod  to one of the most famous members of the  bat family nightwing by the end of the  batman catwoman aka selena kyle decides  that it's time for her to leave gotham  for a while it's an understandable move  because part of her arc revolves around  finding who killed her best friend  annika and why  to make matters worse selena is forced  to confront the fact that she's the  illegitimate daughter of mobster carmine  falcone he abandoned celina's mother  after their brief fling and she was  forced to grow up in poverty as a result  falcone meanwhile only grew more  powerful  so after she helps batman stop the  riddler's plan she tells the dark knight  she might head to bloodhaven that's a  loaded reference for comics readers  bloodhaven is a city not too far from  gotham it's also where dick grayson who  became nightwing after being robin moves  in the comics when he starts to forge  his own identity away from batman  pranks jokes and tomfoolery have no  place here and my identity must reflect  that from this day forward  call me nightwing as he soon finds out  bloodhaven is an incredibly violent  place and there aren't any superheroes  operating there because of how ruthless  the villains are nightwing is the one  who makes a stand when bruce asks him to  investigate a string of deaths in 1996's  nightwing issue number one it's not  enough for dick just to patrol the  streets at night though as he needs  reliable intelligence to take down  gangsters like blockbuster even ends up  becoming a police officer by day while  it's entirely possible that reeves and  his co-writer peter craig will introduce  dick grayson further down the line the  bloodhaven reference probably isn't a  hint that nightwing will show up in the  batman 2. even if they introduce grayson  in the sequel he'll probably start off  as robin to explore that dynamic with  batman rather than stepping into his  nightwing persona straight away  name-dropping bloodhaven is more likely  just a bit of world building however  that's not to say nightwing won't make  the leap to the big screen eventually  warner brothers picked the tomorrow war  director chris mckay to helm a solo  movie for the hero in the dc extended  universe when speaking to den of geek  back in 2021 mckay said he still wants  to work on the project i hope that we  get a chance to go out and make that  dick grace in a nightwing film a  particular part of robin growing from  being under batman to becoming nightwing  and bloodhaven and all that stuff it's a  really personal story to me for  nightwing fans desperate to see the hero  in live action at least hbo max's titans  will scratch that itch brenton thwaites  plays a version of the hero that's  become a real fan favorite and it's not  hard to see why  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  the batman are coming soon subscribe to  our youtube channel and hit the bell so  you don't miss a single one  [Music]

